From: programista-zacny <5969291+programista-zacny@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] config: allow keeping ro.debuggable in userdebug with secured adb

Without WITH_ADB_INSECURE, common.mk sets PRODUCT_NOT_DEBUGGABLE_IN_USERDEBUG
:= true, so a userdebug build gets ro.debuggable=0: "Rooted debugging"
disappears and adb root is impossible. Setting the variable to "false" in a
device makefile does not help, because add_json_bool (build/make/common/
json.mk) treats every non-empty value as true, and an empty single-value
product variable falls back to the inherited value.

Add a switch: with LINEAGE_KEEP_DEBUGGABLE_IN_USERDEBUG=true in the
environment the variable is not set, ro.debuggable stays 1, adb still
requires authorization (ro.adb.secure=1) and root over adb still requires
"Rooted debugging" in Developer options. The gts210ltexx build script
exports it, because root over adb is how this port is diagnosed.
---
diff --git a/config/common.mk b/config/common.mk
index 3f9b089..f67ea2d 100644
--- a/config/common.mk
+++ b/config/common.mk
@@ -39,9 +39,12 @@ else
 # Enable ADB authentication
 PRODUCT_SYSTEM_EXT_PROPERTIES += ro.adb.secure=1
 
-# Set ro.debuggable=0 for userdebug
+# Set ro.debuggable=0 for userdebug, unless the build keeps it: adb still needs the computer
+# to be authorized, and root over adb still needs "Rooted debugging" in Developer options.
+ifneq ($(LINEAGE_KEEP_DEBUGGABLE_IN_USERDEBUG),true)
 PRODUCT_NOT_DEBUGGABLE_IN_USERDEBUG := true
 endif
+endif
 
 # Disable extra StrictMode features on all non-engineering builds
 PRODUCT_PRODUCT_PROPERTIES += persist.sys.strictmode.disable=true
